    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pairs\n\n### Description\n\nwhen trying to insert any paired symbols, an error message would pop up and a 0 will inserted instead.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nv0.9.5\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. setup mini.pairs in config\r\n2. restart nvim\r\n3. try to input any paired symbols, like \"(\".\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nan error message will show up, and a 0 will be inserted instead.\r\n<img width=\"1500\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/128014942/d8f171ba-9f95-4c36-af1e-e956465f26fe\">",
